  "title": "indigo_agent_scheduler: fix the hook task list and history labels described in the scheduler guide",
  "description": "INDIGO_SCHEDULER_GUIDE.md, section on hooks (around line 577-579), describes the task list and history labels of hook tasks incorrectly:\n- It says the task list shows a hook task as `STARTUP HOOK`, `SHUTDOWN HOOK`, ... but the AGENT_SCHEDULER_TASK_STATE label has the state `HOOK` and the hook kind in the priority column, e.g. `Park | HOOK | hook shutdown | - | - | -` (`hook startup`, `hook shutdown`, `hook idle`, `hook night start`, `hook night end`, `hook resume`, or `hook` for an unassigned @hook task).\n- It says hook runs appear in the history marked `(hook)`, but the history label has `hook` in its kind column.\nDocumentation-only fix; no code change.",
  "type": "change",
