          "outcome": {
            "summary": "Diff (INDIGO_SCHEDULER_GUIDE.md lines 577, 579) matches the code. Task list: build_task_state_label() sets state HOOK for is_hook() tasks and blank runs/retries/duration, which join_label() renders as '-'; task_priority_text() returns 'hook startup'..'hook resume' from hook_names[] in the listed order, so 'Park | HOOK | hook shutdown | - | - | -' is exact. History: history_label() puts 'hook' in the 4th (kind) column for mark 'H'. Wording agrees with the guide's task-list example and priority text (~753-758), the state table HOOK row (~776), the history section kind column (~795) and SCHEDULER.md Hooks (line 520, 522). Non-blocking note: line 577 lists only the named-hook priorities, not plain 'hook' for an unnamed @hook task; that case is documented at ~758 and in SCHEDULER.md:520, and the 577 bullet is about tasks named by hooks, so this is not a defect. No other findings.",
